hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16730","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-Ashath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from a man from Banu Yarbu, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him addressing the people saying: The hand of the giver is the upper; your mother and your father and your sister and your brother, then the nearest then the nearest; he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Thalaba who struck so-and-so; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, no soul wrongs on behalf of another."
